  "decision": "done",
  "reason": "The patch normalizes option strings when storing them in the parser's lookup dictionaries (_short_opt and _long_opt). This fixes the root cause: when options are declared with capital letters (like '--Greeting' or '-N'), they are now stored under their normalized keys (like '--greeting' or '-n'). When users provide input on the command line, it's also normalized before lookup, so the keys match. This allows options declared with capitals to be provided in any case (--greeting, --GREETING, --Greeting all work), and the same for short options (-n, -N both work). The fix directly addresses all three error cases mentioned in the bug report."
}
```

